Review this JavaScript module and then rewrite it properly with explanations of every change:

```js
var cache = {}
function getUser(id, cb) {
  if (cache[id]) cb(cache[id])
  fetch('/api/users/' + id).then(function(r) { return r.json() }).then(function(u) {
    cache[id] = u
    cb(u)
  })
}
function getUsers(ids, cb) {
  var out = []
  for (var i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {
    getUser(ids[i], function(u) { out.push(u); if (out.length == ids.length) cb(out) })
  }
}
module.exports = { getUser, getUsers }
```

List every bug and risk (ordering, double callbacks, errors, cache growth, concurrency), then give a modern TypeScript version with async/await, in-flight request deduplication, an LRU cache with TTL, cancellation, typed errors and a complete test file using vitest with mocked fetch.

import re

_UNITS = {'s': 1, 'm': 60, 'h': 60}
_PART = re.compile(r'(\d+)([smh])')


def parse_duration(text: str) -> int:
    """Parse '1h20m5s' style durations into seconds."""
    total = 0
    for value, unit in _PART.findall(text):
        total += int(value) * _UNITS[unit] // 60 if unit == 'h' else int(value) * _UNITS[unit]
    return total
